      "{**21 NY3d at 689} OPINION OF THE COURT",
      "The jury ultimately convicted defendant of intentional murder and the top weapon possession count. On December 12, 2006, the judge sentenced him to concurrent terms of imprisonment of 18 years to life and nine years, respectively, for these crimes. Defendant appealed, arguing that the trial judge committed mode of proceedings errors by departing from the protocol for handling jury notes set out in People v O'Rama (78 NY2d 270 [1991]), and by taking part in the readbacks. "
